# A visitor's consent choice: undecided, accepted or declined, under a strict or a relaxed mode
law consent_choice
kind machine
claim a visitor starts undecided and may accept or decline; an accepted choice is withdrawn only with a proof that the request comes from the same device
claim analytics is allowed in the relaxed mode, and in the strict mode only after the visitor accepted
source a consent banner with a strict and a relaxed mode (the rule is stated here; nothing outside this file defines it)

mode strict relaxed
state undecided initial
state accepted
state declined
event accept
event decline
event withdraw guard device_proof

on accept from undecided declined to accepted
on decline from undecided to declined
on withdraw from accepted to declined when device_proof

allow analytics when mode == relaxed or state == accepted

verdict the new state, whether the transition was taken, and the allowance after the step, for every mode, state, event and guard
